    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras face a high-upside slate today, anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) and **Yordan Alvarez** (77.56). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our premier play, leveraging his elite sprint speed against a slow-delivery pitcher; the 14% platoon adjustment and 4% stolen base synergy make him a must-start as we hunt for the scarcest category in 5x5 Roto. **Yordan Alvarez** remains the model of consistency with an elite .458 xwOBA, while **Junior Caminero** (76.90) slots into the heart of the order with a prime matchup against Jobe, benefiting from a 5% park factor boost and strong order placement. These three represent our highest probability of driving positive variance in R and RBI production today.\n\nThe most difficult benching decision involved **Chase Meidroth** (37.20), who narrowly missed our 40.0 floor due to a brutal matchup against deGrom. The 19% penalty applied for the pitcher\u2019s skill level effectively neutralized any potential gains, pushing him to the pine in favor of the higher-floor, mid-tier starts like **Jacob Gonzalez** (47.71). We are also navigating a volatile environment for **Trea Turner** (60.02) and **Kyle Schwarber** (59.47), both of whom face Kirby. While both are cleared to start, their scores are dampened by a 5% negative park factor and the general toughness of the matchup. We have opted to play them for their speed and power ceilings, respectively, but they require close monitoring if early-inning weather risks escalate. While **Gary Sanchez** (56.17) and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (54.86) provide decent platoon-based value against Liberatore, they remain mid-tier pivots that we will rely on to maintain our categorical balance rather than provide explosive scoring.",
